From a68451ab1e5227372b99f6007d238b9f92975ff6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <blue@aquarat.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:03:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(ml): add libclipvit, a ggml-based CLIP image encoder

Adds machine-learning/ggml, a small C++ library on the public ggml API that
runs an open_clip VisionTransformer (patch conv, class/positional embeddings,
ln_pre, residual attention blocks with fused QKV, ln_post on the class token
and the visual projection) from a GGUF file on a ggml backend. ggml and its
Vulkan backend are linked statically, so the runtime only needs
libclipvit.so, the Vulkan loader and the host's driver.

The C API (clipvit.h) loads a model onto a GPU device (or the CPU), encodes
preprocessed NCHW float32 images into L2-normalised embeddings, and reports
the embedding size, image size, device and unsupported ops. clipvit-cli is a
small driver for tests and benchmarks. build.sh mirrors ann/build.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VXX3uBLex4GVki947Lm5qV
